# Environment configuration — Learning Adventures campus demo
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values.
#
# Every variable below is one this tree actually reads. The file it is read
# from is named next to it, so you can check rather than trust this list.
#
# Note the campus demo itself (/dev/campus-sandbox) needs NONE of these — the
# world, NPCs and HUD are all client-side Phaser with no backend. These are
# for the rest of the app that ships alongside it: the auth UI layer, the
# Prisma-backed pages, the child-session routes, and the agent tooling.

# ─── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The auth layer. Read by lib/supabase/{client,server,middleware}.ts and
# hooks/useAuth.ts. The two NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are exposed to the browser by
# design — they are the publishable anon pair, not secrets.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is required in the browser on a secure context; the
# client calls createBrowserClient(url!, anonKey!) with no fallback, so a
# missing value surfaces as a runtime error rather than a graceful degrade.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key-here

# Server-only. Read by lib/supabase/server.ts (admin client) and prisma/seed.ts.
# This one IS a secret — it bypasses row-level security. Never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit a real value.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-supabase-service-role-key-here

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by prisma/schema.prisma, not by application code:
#   url = env("DATABASE_URL"), directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")
# `npm run build` runs `prisma generate` first, so these matter at build time.
# DIRECT_URL is the non-pooled connection Prisma uses for migrations.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/learning_adventures
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/learning_adventures

# ─── Child sessions (COPPA-compliant child accounts) ─────────────────────────
# Read by lib/childAuth.ts, which THROWS AT MODULE SCOPE if it is unset. Next
# imports every route module when collecting page data, so an unset value
# fails `next build` outright rather than only at runtime. That guard is
# deliberate: a child session token signed with a default or guessable key is
# worth less than no token at all.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
CHILD_SESSION_SECRET=your-child-session-secret-here

# ─── Anthropic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by lib/claude-client.ts and lib/anthropic/client.ts for the content
# generation tooling. Not needed to run the campus demo.
# Get a key from: https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# ─── Removed from this file, and why ─────────────────────────────────────────
# These were documented here but are read nowhere in this tree. Grep before
# re-adding any of them:
#
#   NEXTAUTH_URL, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   APPLE_CLIENT_ID, APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET, EMAIL_SERVER_*, EMAIL_FROM
#       NextAuth configuration. The app moved to Supabase + jose; next-auth is
#       not a dependency and nothing imports it.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY
#       Documented as required for a "Gemini 3 Content Studio" that does not
#       exist in this tree.
#
#   COOKIE_DOMAIN
#       Cross-subdomain cookie setting for the NextAuth era. Unused.
